h3("Pre-booking the maintenance calendar months ahead");
p("The strongest spas do not book one visit at a time. They map the patient's maintenance calendar months in advance, so standing appointments are locked in and the schedule fills itself. Do this at every check-out for any patient on a maintenance rhythm.");
microLabel("Say");
scriptBox([
  "Let's do something that'll make your life so much easier. Instead of booking one visit at a time, let's go ahead and put your next few appointments on the calendar now, spaced out over the coming months exactly the way [Provider] wants to see you. That way you always have your ideal time, you never fall behind on your results, and you don't have to think about it. I'll set them all up, and you can shift any of them if life happens. Sound good?"
]);
why("Booking several months of visits at once locks in revenue, guarantees the patient stays on the schedule their results require, and removes the friction of rebooking from scratch every time. Patients welcome it because it takes the planning off their plate.");

